      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Since $\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M} = \\mathbf{I},$ we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M} &= \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & x & x \\\\ 2y & y & -y \\\\ z & -z & z \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 2y & z \\\\ x & y & -z \\\\ x & -y & z \\end{pmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{pmatrix} 2x^2 + 2x^2 & 2y^2 + xy - y^2 & xy - zx + xz \\\\\n2xy + 2y^2 & 4y^2 + (-y) + y^2 & 2yz + zy + (-zy) \\\\\n2zx + zx & 2yz + (-y) + zy & 3z^2 + z^2 + z^2\n\\end{pmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{pmatrix} 4x^2 & xy + y^2 & xy - zx + xz \\\\\n2xy + 2y^2 & 4y^2 & 2yz \\\\\n4z^2 & 2yz & 6z^2\n\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\end{align*}Therefore,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\begin{pmatrix} 4x^2 & xy + y^2 & xy - zx + xz \\\\\n2xy + 2y^2 & 4y^2 & 2yz \\\\\n4z^2 & 2yz & 6z^2\n\\end{pmatrix} &= \\text{The identity matrix}. \\\\\n(x^2 + y^2 + z^2) \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\n\\end{pmatrix} &= \\text{The identity matrix}. \\\\\nx^2 + y^2 + z^2 &= \\boxed{1}.\n\\end{align*}.  We find that $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = p$ and the required boxed answer is $p.$",
